## Test Anti-Pattern Audit — Severity-Ranked Findings

This test file is a textbook example of **"coverage without verification"** — every production method is invoked (achieving line coverage) but almost nothing meaningful is asserted.

---

### 🔴 Critical — Tests that verify nothing

| # | Test | Anti-Pattern | Production Bug Risk |
|---|------|-------------|-------------------|
| 1 | `AddProduct_Works` (L17) | **No assertion at all.** Calls `AddProduct` then exits. | Product could silently fail to persist. |
| 2 | `UpdatePrice_Works` (L33) | **No assertion.** Calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the price changed. | Price update could save wrong value (e.g., `p.Price * newPrice`) and this test passes. |
| 3 | `RemoveProduct_Works` (L39) | **No assertion.** Never verifies the product is actually gone. | `Delete` could be a no-op. |
| 4 | `GetProductCount_Works` (L64) | **No assertion, no setup.** Discards return value. | Count logic could return -1 and pass. |
| 5 | `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (L69) | **No assertion.** Never checks resulting prices. | Discount formula `Price * (1 - fraction)` could be `Price * fraction` — this test can't tell. |
| 6 | `ImportFromCsv_Works` (L85) | **No assertion.** Never checks products were stored. | Parsing bugs (wrong column order, culture-specific decimals) are invisible. |

### 🟠 High — Assertions that are technically present but meaningless

| # | Test | Anti-Pattern | Fix |
|---|------|-------------|-----|
| 7 | `GetProduct_Works` (L26) | **`Assert.IsNotNull` on a reference that's trivially non-null.** Never checks `Sku`, `Name`, or `Price`. | Assert field equality: `Assert.AreEqual("Widget", result.Name)` |
| 8 | `SearchProducts_Works` (L48) | **`Assert.IsNotNull` on a `List<>` (never null).** Never checks count or content. | Assert `results.Count == 1` and `results[0].Sku == "SKU-001"` |
| 9 | `ExportToCsv_Works` (L78) | **`Assert.IsNotNull` on a `string` (never null from `string.Join`).** Never validates format. | Assert `StringAssert.Contains(csv, "SKU-001,Widget,9.99")` |
| 10 | `GetAllProducts_Works` (L56) | Same as #8 — `IsNotNull` on a guaranteed non-null list. | Assert `all.Count == 1` |

### 🟡 Medium — Missing negative/edge-case paths

| # | Missing Test | Risk |
|---|-------------|------|
| 11 | `UpdatePrice` with non-existent SKU | `KeyNotFoundException` path is never exercised; callers may not handle it. |
| 12 | `GetProduct` returns `null` | Null-return path untested — NRE bugs in callers go undetected. |
| 13 | `ImportFromCsv` with malformed input | No coverage for missing columns, bad decimals, empty lines. |
| 14 | `ApplyBulkDiscount` with 0% or >100% | Boundary behavior never tested. |

